<article id="post-1507" class="post-1507 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-uncategorized">
	<header class="entry-header">
							<h1 class="entry-title"><a href="http://cromwellhaus.com/2013/11/find-contact-shortcut-in-skype-for-mac/" rel="bookmark">Find Contact Shortcut in Skype for Mac</a></h1>			</header><!-- .entry-header -->

	
	
	<div class="entry-content">
			<p>It&#8217;s well understood that Skype does not advocate usability, but I won&#8217;t take it anymore.  They have <a href="https://support.skype.com/en/faq/FA12074/what-keyboard-shortcuts-can-i-use-with-skype-for-mac-os-x?&amp;site_preference=normal">some shortcuts</a>, but they&#8217;re pretty pitiful.</p>
<p>I&#8217;m a left hand dominant shortcut-er.  Say what you will about me, but I can&#8217;t make my fingers use <code>CMD+OPTION+F</code> for finding a contact to start a new conversation.  So I created the following shortcut.<br />
<a href="http://cromwellhaus.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/2013-11-26_11-28-45.png"><img class=" wp-image-1508 alignleft" alt="mac-skype-find-shortcut" src="http://cromwellhaus.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/2013-11-26_11-28-45.png" width="668" height="598" srcset="http://cromwellhaus.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/2013-11-26_11-28-45.png 668w, http://cromwellhaus.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/11/2013-11-26_11-28-45-300x268.png 300w" sizes="(max-width: 668px) 100vw, 668px" /></a></p>
				</div><!-- .entry-content -->

